<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! library.collection.shows ~ one collection, body by body

`lares library show <collection>` names each body of one collection: its real filename, size, media type, integrity anchor and recorded origin (an unrecorded origin says so out loud). The collection name reads lowercased; a name the shelf holds no directory for refuses.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ one-collection

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`one-collection` params=`collection/mark-twain ~ the bodies of one collection`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ collection

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`collection` params=`takes/name needs/required seat/1 as/<collection> ~ the collection, lowercased`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ local

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`local` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ reads this host's own library home; this handler checks no ocap`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ usage

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`usage` params=`cure/[[library.shelf.lists]] ~ no collection named, or none of that name on this shelf; list the shelf`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ shown

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`shown` params=`exit/0 fields/[[collection ref dir entries]] ~ the collection's bodies and the directory that holds them`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

